# /runaway-stopper: detect, stop, prevent

Needs Capy's thread and subagent tools. Steps 1 and 2 only read. Stop only your own subagents; only a Captain
rotates and archives, and only threads in its own crew (R39). An org sweep runs Step 1 everywhere and sends each
finding to the owning Captain; threads outside every crew are left alone.

## 1. Detect

Fetch and scan in one execute program, so nothing large enters your context:

```js
const dir = "/home/user/.capy/work/runaway/" + new Date(await now()).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
const pages = 3; // 1 for an org sweep; empty_wake needs 20+ turns, else it prints "unmeasured"
const list = await tools.thread.list({ scope: "crew", status: ["working", "waiting", "idle"], limit: 100 }); // org sweep: scope "all"
for (const code of [...list.items.map(t => t.code), "this"]) {
  let before, items = [], doc;
  for (let k = 0; k < pages; k++) {
    const g = await tools.thread.get({ thread_id: code, transcript: { limit: 100, tools: true, before } });
    const { transcript, recent, ...rest } = g; doc ??= rest;
    items.push(...transcript.items.map(i => ({ source: i.source, tool: i.tool, calls: i.calls, createdAt: i.createdAt,
      input: i.input && { text: String(i.input.text ?? "").slice(0, 300) } })));
    if (!(before = transcript.beforeCursor)) break;
  }
  await tools.capy.write({ path: `${dir}/${doc.code}.thread.json`, content: JSON.stringify(doc) });
  await tools.capy.write({ path: `${dir}/${doc.code}.events.json`, content: JSON.stringify(items) });
}
return (await tools.capy.bash({ command: `~/.claude/skills/gstack/bin/gstack-runaway scan --dir ${dir}`, description: "Scanning" })).output;
```

On a lane with nested subagents, also write `tools.subagent.list()` to `<code>.subagents.json`: it lists the
whole tree, where thread.get lists direct children only (200 at most, so `own` is then an upper bound).

Limits (org rule R70): own tokens (total minus subagents) past 500M, or active (working, waiting, or a turn in the
last 24 hours) past 3 days: rotate, warn at 400M. A subagent past 100M: stop and look. Empty wakes past 25% of the
last 40 turns. Review rounds past 2 per PR. Act on each line:

| Line | Do |
|---|---|
| `FLAG: ROTATE` | Step 3. |
| `FLAG: REPORT` | A Captain over a limit: report it, never rotate it (Garry decides Captain rotation). |
| `FLAG: STOP` | Step 2. |
| `FLAG: LOOK` | A finished subagent past 100M: find why (reused for several runs? full-depth review?) and fix that cause from Step 4. |
| `FLAG: WARN` | Tell the thread the Step 4 rule it breaks, once. |
| `DEFER:` | The thread is mid-/ship or mid-merge: act on nothing now; scan again when that work finishes. |

## 2. Stop a subagent

Your own: `tools.subagent.stop({ paths: ["<path>"] })`, and record the reason: "<tokens> > 100M (R70), <what it was
doing>". A crew thread's subagent: send that thread one message, "Stop Subagent <path>: <tokens> > 100M (R70)." Its
PR stays open; a fresh subagent with the run directory picks the work up if it is still needed.

## 3. Rotate a thread

Rotate only at a clean point: no `DEFER:`, no READY of that thread waiting on you, no merge in flight for its PR.
1. Tell it: "Rotation (R70). Start nothing new; write handoffs/<code>-rotation.md from gstack's
   `runaway-stopper/templates/rotation-handoff.md` and reply with its path."
2. Start the successor in your crew from `runaway-stopper/templates/successor-brief.md` (a lane asks its Captain, R68).
3. Once the successor reports, archive the old thread: `tools.thread.archive({ threads: ["<code>"] })`.

## 4. Prevent

Put the lines that apply into every brief you write:
- **One wait.** Register one `wait` on every pending operation (`return_when: "all"` when you need them all).
  Subagent completions wake you on their own: never add a wait or a poll for them.
- **Quiet wakes.** A wake with nothing to decide ends with `end_turn`. No acknowledgment, "working" or progress
  message to a parent or Captain: send a READY, a decision you need, a blocker or the final report.
- **Compact returns.** A program returns only the lines the next step needs; big output goes to a file under
  ~/.capy/work and you read the part you need.
- **One /ship subagent per PR head.** A rerun or another PR gets a fresh subagent with the run directory path; never
  message a finished /ship subagent to run another. A /ship subagent gets an 80M cap by default
  (`BUDGET_DEFAULT_CAP:`); raising it needs the owner's words.
- **Two review rounds.** Reader and review rounds stop at 2 per PR (R51), and every reader's title names the PR
  (`#<n>`) so the scan can count them.
- **Rotate standing roles** at 500M own tokens or 3 days. An automation gets a fresh thread per run that archives
  itself, or a slower schedule, instead of waking a standing thread.

## Report

Paste the `RUNAWAY:`, `FLAG:`, `DEFER:` and `SWEEP:` lines verbatim, then one line per flag: stopped (path),
rotated (successor code), deferred (until what) or told (thread).
